 "text": "Hey there! How's your day so far? An SSD stores data in flash memory chips, while a hard drive uses spinning disks. SSDs are much faster at loading things and switching between them. Very. With an SSD, apps open in just a few seconds, games load instantly, and gaming PCs really shine. For a laptop, two or four gigabytes is plenty for most people. More is needed only for handling lots of videos or games. Cloud storage is separate from the SSD, so it doesn't change how much space you have on your laptop.",
